      "finding_1_title": "Blinkit Store Expansion vs. Store-Level Throughput Maturation",
      "derived_calculations": "Throughput per store-day = NOV * 10^7 / (Period-End Stores * 91.25). In Q1 FY25, Blinkit Net Order Value (NOV) was \u20b94,061.0 Cr across 639 period-end dark stores, yielding an average throughput of \u20b9696,465 (~\u20b96.96 lakh) per store-day. By Q2 FY27, dark stores quadrupled (+322.5% to 2,700 stores) while NOV expanded to \u20b920,940.0 Cr (+415.6%), driving average throughput up to \u20b9849,924 (~\u20b98.50 lakh) per store-day (+22.0% throughput expansion). [AUDIT NOTE: Prior preliminary drafts erroneously plugged in Swiggy Instamart's GOV of \u20b92,724 Cr and \u20b99,230 Cr into Blinkit's throughput formula, generating a spurious -20% contraction. Using Blinkit's true disclosed NOV demonstrates robust +22.0% throughput expansion despite massive store footprint scaling].",
